Below is a **GitHub-ready Epic + sub-issues** for adding an **embedded SurrealDB backend** to Prune, with enough **actual code** (Rust + SurrealQL) to start implementing immediately.

This plan assumes:

- SQLite remains the **default** backend (fast, zero-friction).
- SurrealDB becomes an **optional embedded backend** (graph + vectors + full‑text in one store).
- We use **SurrealKV** as the default embedded persistent engine because it’s fully Rust (good for distribution), and **Mem** for tests; optionally allow **RocksDB** for users who want it (but note compile deps).  [oai_citation:0‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealkv)

SurrealDB capabilities we’ll leverage:
- Graph edges with `RELATE` (edges can hold metadata).  [oai_citation:1‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealql/statements/relate)  
- Vector embeddings + HNSW index + `<|k,effort|>` query syntax + `vector::distance::knn()` reuse.  [oai_citation:2‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)  
- Full-text search with analyzers + `BM25`/`HIGHLIGHTS` + `search::score`.  [oai_citation:3‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/full-text-search)  
- Optional hybrid fusion in-db using `search::rrf`.  [oai_citation:4‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)  

---

# Epic: Embedded SurrealDB backend for Prune graphs + embeddings + hybrid search

## Goal
Add a **SurrealDB embedded backend** so Prune can store:

- fragments (text + metadata)
- embeddings per fragment
- graph relations (imports/refs/defines/calls/etc.)
- optional full-text index + BM25 scoring
- optional hybrid retrieval (vector + lexical fusion)

…while keeping SQLite as the default backend.

## Why
This enables “one store” workflows:
- Graph traversal queries
- Vector KNN similarity
- Full text search / scoring
- Hybrid retrieval (optionally inside DB)

SurrealDB supports all of these in a unified engine.  [oai_citation:5‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)

## Non-goals
- Not replacing Prune’s AST slicing, pack budgeting, or strategy evolution logic
- Not running SurrealDB as a network server (this epic is **embedded**)
- Not supporting multi-user sync/conflict resolution

## Deliverables
- New optional backend: `--store surreal`
- Embedded persistent engine: `surrealkv://…` by default
- Parity with existing index/search/pack behaviors
- Benchmarks + tests that compare to SQLite backend

---

# Sub-issue 1: Storage abstraction so Prune can swap backends

## Summary
Introduce a small “store API” trait used by indexing + retrieval, implemented by:
- existing SQLite store
- new SurrealDB store

## Files
- `crates/ce-store-core/src/lib.rs` (new)
- `crates/ce-store-sqlite/…` (adapter wrapper around existing DB)
- `crates/ce-store-surreal/…` (new)

## Code: `ce-store-core` trait
```rust
// crates/ce-store-core/src/lib.rs
use async_trait::async_trait;
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};

#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct RepoIdentity {
    pub repo_id: String,      // e.g. hash of repo root contents
    pub root_path: String,    // absolute path for local-only use
    pub default_branch: Option<String>,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct FileRecord {
    pub file_id: String,      // stable id (e.g. hash(repo_id + path))
    pub repo_id: String,
    pub path: String,
    pub lang: String,         // "rust" | "ts" | "tsx" | "swift" | ...
    pub blob_hash: String,    // content hash
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct FragmentRecord {
    pub frag_id: String,      // stable id (hash of file + span + kind)
    pub repo_id: String,
    pub file_id: String,
    pub kind: String,         // "api_summary" | "function" | "type" | ...
    pub symbol: Option<String>,
    pub start_line: u32,
    pub end_line: u32,
    pub text: String,
    pub embedding: Option<Vec<f32>>,
    pub token_estimate: Option<u32>,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct EdgeRecord {
    pub repo_id: String,
    pub from_id: String,      // record id (file_id or frag_id or symbol_id)
    pub edge_type: String,    // "ts_import" | "defines" | "refs" | ...
    pub to_id: String,
    pub weight: f32,
    pub meta: serde_json::Value,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct SearchHit {
    pub frag_id: String,
    pub score: f32,
    pub reason: String,       // "vector" | "fts" | "hybrid"
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct PackRequest {
    pub repo_id: String,
    pub query: String,
    pub k: usize,
    pub token_budget: usize,
    pub include_kinds: Vec<String>,
    pub expand_edges: Vec<String>,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct PackResult {
    pub fragments: Vec<FragmentRecord>,
    pub total_tokens_estimate: usize,
    pub debug: serde_json::Value,
}

#[async_trait]
pub trait CeStore: Send + Sync {
    async fn init_repo(&self, repo: &RepoIdentity) -> anyhow::Result<()>;

    async fn upsert_files(&self, files: &[FileRecord]) -> anyhow::Result<()>;
    async fn upsert_fragments(&self, frags: &[FragmentRecord]) -> anyhow::Result<()>;
    async fn upsert_edges(&self, edges: &[EdgeRecord]) -> anyhow::Result<()>;

    async fn delete_missing_files(&self, repo_id: &str, keep_file_ids: &[String]) -> anyhow::Result<usize>;
    async fn delete_missing_fragments(&self, repo_id: &str, keep_frag_ids: &[String]) -> anyhow::Result<usize>;

    async fn vector_search(&self, repo_id: &str, query_vec: &[f32], k: usize) -> anyhow::Result<Vec<SearchHit>>;
    async fn fts_search(&self, repo_id: &str, query: &str, k: usize) -> anyhow::Result<Vec<SearchHit>>;
    async fn hybrid_search_rrf(&self, repo_id: &str, query: &str, query_vec: &[f32], k: usize) -> anyhow::Result<Vec<SearchHit>>;

    async fn fetch_fragments(&self, repo_id: &str, frag_ids: &[String]) -> anyhow::Result<Vec<FragmentRecord>>;
    async fn expand_graph(&self, repo_id: &str, seed_ids: &[String], edge_types: &[String], max_nodes: usize) -> anyhow::Result<Vec<String>>;

    async fn pack(&self, req: PackRequest) -> anyhow::Result<PackResult>;
}
```

## Acceptance criteria
- Indexing and packing code depends on `CeStore` only
- SQLite backend still works unchanged (adapter)
- New backend can be added without touching indexer logic

