# Sub-issue 2: Add embedded SurrealDB backend crate

## Summary
Create `ce-store-surreal` implementing `CeStore` using embedded SurrealDB.

We will support engine selection:
- `mem` (tests)
- `surrealkv` default persistent engine
- optional `rocksdb` for users who prefer it

Embedded mode is supported by SurrealDB’s Rust SDK.  [oai_citation:6‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/embedding/rust)  
SurrealKV is file-backed and Rust-native, but the SurrealKV docs note it’s considered beta.  [oai_citation:7‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealkv)  
RocksDB is common but may require external deps and can be heavy to compile.  [oai_citation:8‡Docs.rs](https://docs.rs/surrealdb/latest/surrealdb/engine/any/index.html)

## Cargo features
Add behind a feature flag so default builds stay lean:

```toml
# crates/ce-store-surreal/Cargo.toml
[features]
default = []
surreal = []

[dependencies]
anyhow = "1"
async-trait = "0.1"
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
serde_json = "1"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["rt-multi-thread", "macros"] }

# behind feature "surreal"
surrealdb = { version = "2", default-features = false, features = ["kv-mem", "surreal-kv"], optional = true }
```

Notes:
- SurrealDB embedded examples use `Surreal::new::<Mem>(())` and also show local engines like RocksDB.  [oai_citation:9‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/embedding/rust)  
- SurrealKV with versioning is shown using `SurrealKv` and `.versioned()`.  [oai_citation:10‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/sdk/rust/methods/new)

## Code: Surreal store config + connector
```rust
// crates/ce-store-surreal/src/lib.rs
use anyhow::Context;
use surrealdb::Surreal;

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub enum SurrealEngine {
    Mem,
    SurrealKv { path: String, versioned: bool },
    // Optional later:
    // RocksDb { path: String },
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct SurrealConfig {
    pub ns: String,
    pub db: String,
    pub engine: SurrealEngine,
    pub embedding_dim: usize,
}

pub struct SurrealStore {
    pub cfg: SurrealConfig,
    pub db: Surreal<surrealdb::engine::any::Any>,
}

impl SurrealStore {
    pub async fn connect(cfg: SurrealConfig) -> anyhow::Result<Self> {
        // We use Surreal<Any> so we can select engine by endpoint string at runtime.  [oai_citation:11‡Docs.rs](https://docs.rs/surrealdb/latest/surrealdb/engine/any/index.html)
        let endpoint = match &cfg.engine {
            SurrealEngine::Mem => "mem://".to_string(),
            SurrealEngine::SurrealKv { path, versioned } => {
                if *versioned {
                    format!("surrealkv+versioned://{}", path)
                } else {
                    format!("surrealkv://{}", path)
                }
            }
        };

        let db = surrealdb::engine::any::connect(endpoint).await
            .context("Failed to connect to embedded SurrealDB")?;

        db.use_ns(&cfg.ns).use_db(&cfg.db).await
            .context("Failed to select namespace/db")?;

        Ok(Self { cfg, db })
    }
}
```

## Acceptance criteria
- `SurrealStore::connect` works for `mem://` and `surrealkv://…`
- CI tests can run with in-memory engine
- Local use can point at `.ce/surreal/` directory and persist across runs

