# Sub-issue 3: Define the Surreal schema (tables + indexes + graph relations)

## Summary
Create a deterministic schema for:
- repos, files, fragments
- optional symbols
- graph edges via `RELATE`
- vector index for embeddings (HNSW)
- full-text index for fragment text (BM25 + optional HIGHLIGHTS)
- optional hybrid fusion helpers

SurrealDB vector docs show defining an HNSW index and querying with `<|k,effort|>` while using `vector::distance::knn()`.  [oai_citation:12‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)  
Full text docs show `DEFINE ANALYZER`, `DEFINE INDEX … FULLTEXT … BM25 HIGHLIGHTS`, and queries using match operators + `search::score`.  [oai_citation:13‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/full-text-search)  
Graph relations are created using `RELATE` and edges can store extra fields.  [oai_citation:14‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealql/statements/relate)

## SurrealQL schema (stored in repo as a .surql file)
Create: `crates/ce-store-surreal/schema/prune.surql`

```sql
-- Namespace/db are selected by the Rust client using use_ns/use_db.

-- Core tables (schemaless is fine for derived index data)
DEFINE TABLE repo SCHEMALESS;
DEFINE TABLE file SCHEMALESS;
DEFINE TABLE frag SCHEMALESS;

-- Optional symbol table
DEFINE TABLE symbol SCHEMALESS;

-- Full-text analyzer for code-ish text
DEFINE ANALYZER code_analyzer
  TOKENIZERS class, blank, punct, camel
  FILTERS lowercase, ascii;

-- Full-text index for fragments (BM25)
DEFINE INDEX frag_text_idx
  ON TABLE frag
  FIELDS text
  FULLTEXT ANALYZER code_analyzer
  BM25;

-- Vector index for embeddings
-- Use DIST COSINE for semantic embeddings; DIMENSION must match embedding model output.  [oai_citation:15‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)
-- TYPE F32 is supported in docs (default is F64).  [oai_citation:16‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)
DEFINE INDEX frag_vec_idx
  ON TABLE frag
  FIELDS embedding
  HNSW DIMENSION $EMBED_DIM DIST COSINE TYPE F32;

-- Helpful field indexes (optional)
DEFINE INDEX file_repo_path ON TABLE file FIELDS repo_id, path;
DEFINE INDEX frag_repo_file ON TABLE frag FIELDS repo_id, file_id;
```

### Notes
- We parameterize `$EMBED_DIM` at install time by text substitution in Rust (or run a second statement).
- If you want `search::highlight`, add `HIGHLIGHTS` to the FTS index.  [oai_citation:17‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/full-text-search)

## Rust code: schema install
```rust
// crates/ce-store-surreal/src/schema.rs
use anyhow::Context;

pub async fn ensure_schema(db: &surrealdb::Surreal<surrealdb::engine::any::Any>, embed_dim: usize) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let raw = include_str!("../schema/prune.surql");
    let rendered = raw.replace("$EMBED_DIM", &embed_dim.to_string());
    db.query(rendered).await.context("Failed to apply schema")?;
    Ok(())
}
```

Call `ensure_schema` in `SurrealStore::connect`.

## Acceptance criteria
- On first run, schema installs cleanly
- On subsequent runs, schema is idempotent (use `OVERWRITE` or tolerate errors)
- Vector KNN queries succeed once embeddings exist
- FTS queries succeed once fragment text exists

