# Sub-issue 4: Write-path implementation (upserts + deletes + batching)

## Summary
Implement upsert paths for files/fragments/edges with batching so indexing stays fast.

We’ll keep record IDs stable:
- `repo:<repo_id>`
- `file:<file_id>`
- `frag:<frag_id>`
- `symbol:<symbol_id>`

## Rust code: upsert fragments (batch)
```rust
// crates/ce-store-surreal/src/write.rs
use anyhow::Context;
use serde_json::json;

pub async fn upsert_fragments(
    db: &surrealdb::Surreal<surrealdb::engine::any::Any>,
    frags: &[ce_store_core::FragmentRecord],
) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    // Batch insert as one query to reduce overhead.
    // Use UPSERT to overwrite by id.
    // We store embedding as an array of numbers; SurrealDB supports numeric arrays for vectors.  [oai_citation:18‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)
    let mut q = String::new();
    for f in frags {
        let rid = format!("frag:{}", f.frag_id);
        let content = json!({
            "repo_id": f.repo_id,
            "file_id": f.file_id,
            "kind": f.kind,
            "symbol": f.symbol,
            "start_line": f.start_line,
            "end_line": f.end_line,
            "text": f.text,
            "embedding": f.embedding.as_ref().map(|v| v.iter().map(|x| *x as f64).collect::<Vec<f64>>()),
            "token_estimate": f.token_estimate,
        });
        q.push_str(&format!("UPSERT {} CONTENT {};\n", rid, content));
    }
    db.query(q).await.context("Failed upserting fragments")?;
    Ok(())
}
```

## Edges via `RELATE`
Graph edges are created with `RELATE` and can contain metadata fields.  [oai_citation:19‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealql/statements/relate)

```rust
pub async fn upsert_edges(
    db: &surrealdb::Surreal<surrealdb::engine::any::Any>,
    edges: &[ce_store_core::EdgeRecord],
) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let mut q = String::new();
    for e in edges {
        // from/to may refer to file or frag or symbol; we prefix by caller contract:
        // e.from_id must already be like "file:..." / "frag:..." / "symbol:..."
        let meta = serde_json::to_string(&e.meta)?;
        q.push_str(&format!(
            "RELATE {}->{}->{} SET repo_id = {}, weight = {}, meta = {};\n",
            e.from_id,
            e.edge_type,
            e.to_id,
            serde_json::to_string(&e.repo_id)?,
            e.weight,
            meta
        ));
    }
    db.query(q).await?;
    Ok(())
}
```

## Deletes (stale cleanup)
Implement `delete_missing_*` with a set-based delete:
- delete where `repo_id = $repo` and `id NOT IN $keep_ids`

## Acceptance criteria
- Indexing completes without per-record round trips
- Stale cleanup works and is fast enough for monorepos
- Edge writes create traversable relations

