# Sub-issue 5: Read-path implementation (vector, FTS, hybrid, graph expansion)

## Summary
Implement:
- vector KNN search
- full-text BM25 search
- hybrid fusion (RRF) optionally inside DB
- graph expansion from seed IDs along edge types

### Vector search
SurrealDB vector docs show:
- `DEFINE INDEX … HNSW DIMENSION …`
- query using `embedding <|k,effort|> $qvec` and reuse distance via `vector::distance::knn()`  [oai_citation:20‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)

```rust
pub async fn vector_search(
    db: &surrealdb::Surreal<surrealdb::engine::any::Any>,
    repo_id: &str,
    qvec: &[f32],
    k: usize,
) -> anyhow::Result<Vec<ce_store_core::SearchHit>> {
    let qvec64: Vec<f64> = qvec.iter().map(|x| *x as f64).collect();
    let sql = r#"
      LET $repo = $repo_id;
      LET $qvec = $qvec;
      SELECT id, vector::distance::knn() AS distance
      FROM frag
      WHERE repo_id = $repo
        AND embedding <|$k,100|> $qvec
      ORDER BY distance ASC
      LIMIT $k;
    "#;
    let mut res = db.query(sql)
        .bind(("repo_id", repo_id))
        .bind(("qvec", qvec64))
        .bind(("k", k as i64))
        .await?;

    #[derive(serde::Deserialize)]
    struct Row { id: String, distance: f64 }

    let rows: Vec<Row> = res.take(0)?;
    Ok(rows.into_iter().map(|r| ce_store_core::SearchHit {
        frag_id: r.id.trim_start_matches("frag:").to_string(),
        score: (1.0 / (1.0 + r.distance)) as f32,
        reason: "vector".to_string(),
    }).collect())
}
```

### Full-text search (BM25 score)
FTS docs show:
- `DEFINE INDEX … FULLTEXT … BM25 HIGHLIGHTS`
- use `@0@` operator to pair with `search::score(0)`  [oai_citation:21‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/full-text-search)

```rust
pub async fn fts_search(
    db: &surrealdb::Surreal<surrealdb::engine::any::Any>,
    repo_id: &str,
    query: &str,
    k: usize,
) -> anyhow::Result<Vec<ce_store_core::SearchHit>> {
    let sql = r#"
      SELECT id, search::score(0) AS score
      FROM frag
      WHERE repo_id = $repo_id
        AND text @0@ $q
      ORDER BY score DESC
      LIMIT $k;
    "#;

    let mut res = db.query(sql)
        .bind(("repo_id", repo_id))
        .bind(("q", query))
        .bind(("k", k as i64))
        .await?;

    #[derive(serde::Deserialize)]
    struct Row { id: String, score: f64 }

    let rows: Vec<Row> = res.take(0)?;
    Ok(rows.into_iter().map(|r| ce_store_core::SearchHit {
        frag_id: r.id.trim_start_matches("frag:").to_string(),
        score: r.score as f32,
        reason: "fts".to_string(),
    }).collect())
}
```

### Hybrid fusion (optional): `search::rrf`
SurrealDB’s vector docs include an example fusing vector + fulltext results via `search::rrf`.  [oai_citation:22‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)

You can implement `hybrid_search_rrf` in-db like:
1) run a vector SELECT list `$vs`
2) run an FTS SELECT list `$ft`
3) `search::rrf([$vs, $ft], $k, 60)`  [oai_citation:23‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealdb/models/vector)

### Graph expansion
Use traversal syntax:
- `SELECT ->edge_type->target FROM record`
or query edge tables produced by `RELATE`.  [oai_citation:24‡SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/docs/surrealql/statements/relate)

Implement expansion as:
- iterative BFS in Rust:
  - for each layer, query outgoing edges of types in `edge_types`
  - accumulate until `max_nodes`

## Acceptance criteria
- vector search returns results with embeddings present
- fts search returns results with text present + index installed
- hybrid returns stable fused results (optional flag)
- graph expansion returns connected neighbors for pack building

